8. Verification Strategy

The APB RAM verification environment uses a combination of directed testing and constrained-random testing.

8.1 Directed Testing

Directed tests target specific DUT features and protocol requirements with deterministic stimuli.

Test ID	Test Name	Objective	Status
DT001	Smoke Test	Basic APB write and read transaction	✅ Complete
DT002	Reset Test	Verify reset initializes the DUT correctly	✅ Complete
DT003	Illegal Address Test	Verify PSLVERR is asserted for invalid addresses	✅ Complete
DT004	Back-to-Back Transaction Test	Verify consecutive APB transfers without errors	✅ Complete
Directed Test Goals
Verify each APB transaction type individually
Validate reset behavior
Verify protocol compliance
Exercise boundary conditions
Verify error handling
8.2 Constrained-Random Testing

Constrained-random tests generate legal APB transactions while randomizing addresses, data, and operation types within defined constraints.

Test ID	Test Name	Objective	Status
CR001	Random Basic Test	Random read/write operations	✅ Complete
CR002	Random Address Test	Random legal addresses	Planned
CR003	Random Data Test	Random data patterns	Planned
CR004	Long Random Regression	Thousands of randomized transactions	Planned
CR005	Random Read/Write Mix	Random operation sequences	Planned
Randomized Fields
Address
Write data
Read/write selection
Transaction sequence
Number of transactions
Constraints
Valid addresses: 0–31
One APB transaction at a time
APB protocol timing maintained
No overlapping transfers
8.3 Future Negative Tests

These intentionally violate assumptions or target corner cases.

Test	Purpose
Invalid Address Burst	Repeated illegal accesses
Reset During Transaction	Reset asserted mid-transfer
Random Reset	Random reset insertion
Boundary Address Test	First and last valid address
